IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), PART VII.1, sections 152.21 to 152.3: the self-employment premium, the
-- return of self-employed earnings, assessment, payment by instalments, interest, penalties, the application of the
-- Income Tax Act, the order in which payments are applied, and refunds of excess premium.
-- Piece ei5, written by the piece agent ei5 (Sonnet 5.5). Layer 1: from the Act's text alone, no point of view.
--
-- The premium rate (s 66 or 66.32, piece ei3), the rate of interest (regulations under s 152.26(5), none found in the
-- Regulations) and the maximum yearly insurable earnings (the keel's s 4) are plain inputs. The calculation of the interest
-- itself is the Income Tax Act's, applied by s 152.28(1), and is not in these texts: the rules here give the amount on which
-- interest is payable and the period (fork F23). Money is a NUMBER of dollars. A premium, penalty or fine is not an
-- amount "equal to a percentage ... of earnings or benefits" in the sense of s 152.01(5) and is not rounded (fork F20).
-- This module imports no other ei5 module.
-- Dates: no enactment or commencement date in these sections; the days in a year on which instalments fall are fixed by
-- the text (15 March, 15 June, 15 September, 15 December; 31 December).

§ `152.21 The self-employment premium`

-- Subsection (2): the amount on which the premium is calculated is the lesser of (a) the person's self-employed earnings
-- for the year and (b) the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year, as calculated under section 4, less the
-- person's insurable earnings (if any).
-- src:2573 | (2) The amount for the purpose of subsection (1) is the lesser of
-- src:2574 | (a) the amount of the person’s self-employed earnings for the year,
-- src:2575 | and
-- src:2576 | (b) the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year, as calculated under section 4, minus the person’s insurable earnings, if any.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.21(2) (src:2573-2576)
GIVEN `the amount of the person's self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER   -- keel: eia-core-maximum-earnings; the published figure is an input
      `the person's insurable earnings for the year, if any` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: Part IV (piece ei3)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.21(2) the amount on which the premium is calculated` IS
    min `the amount of the person's self-employed earnings for the year`
        (`the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` MINUS `the person's insurable earnings for the year, if any`)

-- Subsection (1): the premium is that amount multiplied by the premium rate set under s 66 or 66.32.
-- src:2571 | 152.21 (1) Every self-employed person who has entered into an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1) that has not been terminated or that is not deemed to have been terminated shall, in respect of every year, pay a self-employment premium equal to the amount determined under subsection (2) multiplied by the premium rate set under section 66 or 66.32, as the case may be.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.21(1) (src:2571)
GIVEN `the amount determined under subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium rate set under section 66 or 66.32` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: ss 66 and 66.32 (piece ei3); a rate, 1.64% is 0.0164
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.21(1) the self-employment premium for the year` IS
    `the amount determined under subsection (2)` TIMES `the premium rate set under section 66 or 66.32`

-- Subsections (1) and (3): a person who has entered into an agreement that has not been terminated or deemed terminated
-- pays a premium for every year; for greater certainty a premium is required for the year in which the agreement was
-- entered into, whatever the date, and for the year in which it is terminated or deemed terminated, whatever the date.
-- Read together: a premium is required for each year from the year of entry to the year of termination, both included.
-- src:2571 | 152.21 (1) Every self-employed person who has entered into an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1) that has not been terminated or that is not deemed to have been terminated shall, in respect of every year, pay a self-employment premium equal to the amount determined under subsection (2) multiplied by the premium rate set under section 66 or 66.32, as the case may be.
-- src:2578 | (3) For greater certainty, a premium is required to be paid
-- src:2579 | (a) in respect of the year during which the self-employed person entered into the agreement, regardless of the date on which it was entered into; and
-- src:2580 | (b) in respect of the year during which the agreement is terminated or deemed to be terminated, regardless of the date on which it was terminated or deemed to be terminated.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.21(1) and (3) (src:2571) (src:2578-2580)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the agreement was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the agreement is deemed never to have been entered into` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: none; ei5-agreement s 152.02(7)
      `the day on which the agreement terminated or was deemed to be terminated, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.21(1) and (3) a premium is required to be paid in respect of the year` IF
        NOT (`the agreement is deemed never to have been entered into`)
    AND year AT LEAST `s 2(1) the year containing` `the day on which the agreement was entered into`
    AND `the year is not after the year of termination`
    WHERE
        `the year is not after the year of termination` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the agreement terminated or was deemed to be terminated, if it was`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST t THEN year AT MOST `s 2(1) the year containing` t

§ `152.22 to 152.24 Returns, estimate and assessment`

-- Subsection (1): a person required to pay a premium for a year files, without notice or demand, a return of their self-employed
-- earnings with the Minister of National Revenue, on or before the day on which their income tax return under Part I of the Income
-- Tax Act is required to be filed (or would be required if tax were payable). If the person is unable for any reason to file it,
-- their representative files it.
-- src:2584 | 152.22 (1) If a self-employed person is required to pay a premium for a year in respect of their self-employed earnings, a return of the person’s self-employed earnings for the year shall, without notice or demand for it, be filed with the Minister of National Revenue in the form and manner, and containing the information, specified by that Minister, by that person (or, if the person is unable for any reason to file the return, by their representative) on or before the day on which the person’s return of income under Part I of the Income Tax Act is required by that Part to be filed or would be required by that Part to be filed if tax under that Part were payable for the year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.22(1) (src:2584)
GIVEN `the person is required to pay a premium for the year in respect of their self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person's return of income under Part I of the Income Tax Act is required to be filed, or would be required to be filed if tax were payable for the year` IS A DATE   -- out of range: the Income Tax Act
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 152.22(1) the day on or before which the return of self-employed earnings must be filed without notice or demand` IS
    IF `the person is required to pay a premium for the year in respect of their self-employed earnings`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the person's return of income under Part I of the Income Tax Act is required to be filed, or would be required to be filed if tax were payable for the year`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2584 | 152.22 (1) If a self-employed person is required to pay a premium for a year in respect of their self-employed earnings, a return of the person’s self-employed earnings for the year shall, without notice or demand for it, be filed with the Minister of National Revenue in the form and manner, and containing the information, specified by that Minister, by that person (or, if the person is unable for any reason to file the return, by their representative) on or before the day on which the person’s return of income under Part I of the Income Tax Act is required by that Part to be filed or would be required by that Part to be filed if tax under that Part were payable for the year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.22(1) (src:2584)
GIVEN `the person is unable for any reason to file the return` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.22(1) the person's representative must file the return` IF
    `the person is unable for any reason to file the return`

-- Subsection (2): whether or not the person is liable to pay a premium and whether or not a return has been filed, on demand
-- from the Minister of National Revenue served personally or by registered letter, the person files a return of their earnings
-- from self-employment for the year named in the demand, within any reasonable time the demand specifies. The days count from
-- the day of service (keel fork F4).
-- src:2586 | (2) Whether or not they are liable to pay a premium for a year in respect of their earnings from self-employment and whether or not a return has been filed under subsection (1), every self-employed person shall, on demand from the Minister of National Revenue, served personally or by registered letter, file with that Minister, in the form and containing information specified by that Minister, within any reasonable time that may be specified in the demand, a return of their earnings from self-employment for the year designated in the demand.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.22(2) (src:2586)
GIVEN `the demand was served personally or by registered letter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the demand was served` IS A DATE
      `the reasonable time specified in the demand, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 152.22(2) the day on or before which the return demanded must be filed` IS
    IF `the demand was served personally or by registered letter`
    THEN JUST (`the last day of` `the reasonable time specified in the demand, in days` `days after` `the day on which the demand was served`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (3): every trustee in bankruptcy, assignee, liquidator, curator, receiver, receiver-manager, trustee or committee,
-- and every agent, mandatary or other person administering, managing, winding up, controlling or otherwise dealing with the
-- property, business, estate or succession, or income of a self-employed person who has not filed a return as required, must
-- file a return of the person's self-employed earnings for the year, in the form the Minister specifies.
-- src:2588 | (3) Every trustee in bankruptcy, assignee, liquidator, curator, receiver, receiver-manager trustee or committee and every agent, mandatary or other person administering, managing, winding-up, controlling or otherwise dealing with the property, business, estate or succession, or income of a self-employed person who has not filed a return of the person’s self-employed earnings for a year as required by this section must file with the Minister of National Revenue a return, in the form specified by that Minister, of the person’s self-employed earnings for the year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.22(3) (src:2588)
GIVEN `the person is a trustee in bankruptcy, assignee, liquidator, curator, receiver, receiver-manager, trustee or committee, or an agent, mandatary or other person administering, managing, winding up, controlling or otherwise dealing with the property, business, estate or succession, or income of a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the self-employed person has not filed a return of their self-employed earnings for the year as required by this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.22(3) the administrator of the self-employed person's affairs must file the return` IF
        `the person is a trustee in bankruptcy, assignee, liquidator, curator, receiver, receiver-manager, trustee or committee, or an agent, mandatary or other person administering, managing, winding up, controlling or otherwise dealing with the property, business, estate or succession, or income of a self-employed person`
    AND `the self-employed person has not filed a return of their self-employed earnings for the year as required by this section`

-- src:2590 | (4) The information to be contained in any such return must identify the province in which the self-employed person was resident on the last day of that year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.22(4) (src:2590)
GIVEN `the return identifies the province in which the self-employed person was resident on the last day of that year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.22(4) the return contains the information required` IF
    `the return identifies the province in which the self-employed person was resident on the last day of that year`

-- src:2592 | 152.23 Every self-employed person required by section 152.22 to file a return of their self-employed earnings must, in the return, estimate the amount of the premium to be paid in respect of those earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.23 (src:2592)
GIVEN `the return contains an estimate of the amount of the premium to be paid in respect of those earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.23 the return contains the estimate required` IF
    `the return contains an estimate of the amount of the premium to be paid in respect of those earnings`

-- Section 152.24: the Minister of National Revenue must, with all due dispatch, examine each return, assess the premium and the
-- interest and penalties payable, and send a notice of assessment to the person who filed the return: the person who filed
-- the return is owed the assessment and the notice.
-- src:2594 | 152.24 The Minister of National Revenue must, with all due dispatch, examine each return of self-employed earnings and assess the premium to be paid for the year in respect of those earnings and the interest and penalties, if any, payable, and, after the examination, send a notice of assessment to the person who filed the return.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.24 (src:2594)
GIVEN `a return of self-employed earnings has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.24 the person who filed the return is owed an assessment and a notice of assessment` IF
    `a return of self-employed earnings has been filed`

§ `152.25 Payment of the premium`

-- Subsection (1): a person not required by s 155 or 156 of the Income Tax Act to pay instalments of income tax for the year pays
-- the whole premium on or before their balance-due day for the year.
-- src:2596 | 152.25 (1) A self-employed person shall, on or before their balance-due day for the year, pay to the Receiver General the whole amount of the premium if they are not required by section 155 or 156 of the Income Tax Act to pay instalments for that year in respect of their income tax.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.25(1) (src:2596)
GIVEN `the person is required by section 155 or 156 of the Income Tax Act to pay instalments for that year in respect of their income tax` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the Income Tax Act
      `the person's balance-due day for the year` IS A DATE   -- see s 152.01(1) "balance-due day" in ei5-interpretation
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 152.25(1) the day on or before which the whole premium must be paid` IS
    IF `the person is required by section 155 or 156 of the Income Tax Act to pay instalments for that year in respect of their income tax`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the person's balance-due day for the year`

-- Subsection (2), farmers to whom s 155 of the Income Tax Act applies and who are not under (1): on or before 31 December of
-- the year, two thirds of (a) the premium for the year as the person estimates it, or (b) the premium for the preceding year;
-- the text does not say who chooses between (a) and (b), and the rule lets the person choose (fork F24).
-- src:2597 | Farmers
-- src:2598 | (2) Every self-employed person to whom section 155 of the Income Tax Act applies, other than a person to whom subsection (1) applies, shall pay to the Receiver General on or before December 31 in each year, two thirds of the following amounts:
-- src:2599 | (a) the premium required to be paid by the person for the year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person; or
-- src:2600 | (b) the premium required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the preceding year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.25(2) (src:2597-2600)
GIVEN `the person pays by reference to the premium for the year as estimated by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premium for the year as estimated by the person` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium required in respect of the person's self-employed earnings for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.25(2) the amount payable on or before December 31` IS
    (2 DIVIDED BY 3) TIMES (IF `the person pays by reference to the premium for the year as estimated by the person`
                            THEN `the premium for the year as estimated by the person`
                            ELSE `the premium required in respect of the person's self-employed earnings for the preceding year`)

-- Subsection (3), other persons: on or before 15 March, 15 June, 15 September and 15 December in the year, (a) one quarter of
-- the premium for the year as the person estimates it, or of the premium for the preceding year; or (b) on 15 March and 15 June
-- one quarter of the premium for the second preceding year, and on 15 September and 15 December one half of the excess of the
-- premium for the preceding year over one half of the premium for the second preceding year.
-- src:2602 | Other persons
-- src:2603 | (3) Every self-employed person, other than a person to whom subsection (1) or (2) applies, shall pay to the Receiver General in respect of each year
-- src:2604 | (a) on or before March 15, June 15, September 15 and December 15 in the year, an amount equal to one quarter of
-- src:2605 | (i) the premium required to be paid by the person for the year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person, or
-- src:2606 | (ii) the premium required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the preceding year; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.25(3)(a) (src:2602-2606)
GIVEN `the person pays by reference to the premium for the year as estimated by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premium for the year as estimated by the person` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium required in respect of the person's self-employed earnings for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.25(3)(a) each of the four instalments` IS
    (1 DIVIDED BY 4) TIMES (IF `the person pays by reference to the premium for the year as estimated by the person`
                            THEN `the premium for the year as estimated by the person`
                            ELSE `the premium required in respect of the person's self-employed earnings for the preceding year`)

-- src:2607 | (b) on or before
-- src:2608 | (i) March 15 and June 15 in the year, an amount equal to one quarter of the premium required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the second preceding year, and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.25(3)(b)(i) (src:2607-2608)
GIVEN `the premium required in respect of the person's self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.25(3)(b)(i) each of the instalments of March 15 and June 15` IS
    (1 DIVIDED BY 4) TIMES `the premium required in respect of the person's self-employed earnings for the second preceding year`

-- src:2609 | (ii) September 15 and December 15 in the year, an amount equal to one half of the amount, if any, by which
-- src:2610 | (A) the premium required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the preceding year
-- src:2611 | exceeds
-- src:2612 | (B) one half of the premium required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the second preceding year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.25(3)(b)(ii) (src:2609-2612)
GIVEN `the premium required in respect of the person's self-employed earnings for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium required in respect of the person's self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.25(3)(b)(ii) each of the instalments of September 15 and December 15` IS
    (1 DIVIDED BY 2) TIMES (max 0 (`the premium required in respect of the person's self-employed earnings for the preceding year`
                                    MINUS ((1 DIVIDED BY 2) TIMES `the premium required in respect of the person's self-employed earnings for the second preceding year`)))

-- src:2603 | (3) Every self-employed person, other than a person to whom subsection (1) or (2) applies, shall pay to the Receiver General in respect of each year
-- src:2604 | (a) on or before March 15, June 15, September 15 and December 15 in the year, an amount equal to one quarter of
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.25(3) (src:2603-2604)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
DECIDE `s 152.25(3) the days on or before which the instalments of the year are due` IS
    LIST (YMD year 3 15), (YMD year 6 15), (YMD year 9 15), (YMD year 12 15)

-- Subsections (2) and (3), last sentence: in addition the person pays, on or before their balance-due day, the remainder of
-- the premium as estimated under s 152.23. The paragraphs do not require payment of any amount that would otherwise become
-- due after the person's death.
-- src:2601 | In addition, the person shall pay to the Receiver General, on or before the person’s balance-due day for the year, the remainder of the premium as estimated under section 152.23. However, paragraphs (a) and (b) do not require the payment of any amount in respect of the person that would otherwise become due after the death of the person.
-- src:2613 | In addition, the person shall pay to the Receiver General, on or before the person’s balance-due day for the year, the remainder of the premium as estimated under section 152.23. However, paragraphs (a) and (b) do not require the payment of any amount in respect of the person that would otherwise become due after the death of the person.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.25(2) and (3) (src:2601) (src:2613)
GIVEN `the premium as estimated under section 152.23` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the instalments paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `ss 152.25(2) and (3) the remainder of the premium payable on or before the balance-due day` IS
    max 0 (`the premium as estimated under section 152.23` MINUS `the total of the instalments paid`)

-- src:2601 | In addition, the person shall pay to the Receiver General, on or before the person’s balance-due day for the year, the remainder of the premium as estimated under section 152.23. However, paragraphs (a) and (b) do not require the payment of any amount in respect of the person that would otherwise become due after the death of the person.
-- src:2613 | In addition, the person shall pay to the Receiver General, on or before the person’s balance-due day for the year, the remainder of the premium as estimated under section 152.23. However, paragraphs (a) and (b) do not require the payment of any amount in respect of the person that would otherwise become due after the death of the person.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.25(2) and (3) (src:2601) (src:2613)
GIVEN `the day on or before which the instalment would otherwise become due` IS A DATE
      `the day of the person's death, if the person has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 152.25(2) and (3) the instalment is required` IF
    CONSIDER `the day of the person's death, if the person has died`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST d THEN `the day on or before which the instalment would otherwise become due` AT MOST d

§ `152.26 Interest on unpaid premium`

-- Subsection (1): if the amount paid on or before the balance-due day on account of the premium for the year is less than the
-- premium required, interest is payable at the prescribed rate on the difference from the balance-due day to the day of
-- payment. The rule gives the difference and the period; the interest itself is computed under the Income Tax Act as s 152.28(1)
-- applies it (fork F23). No rate is prescribed in the Regulations as deposited.
-- src:2615 | 152.26 (1) If the amount paid by a self-employed person on or before the person’s balance-due day for a year on account of the premium required to be paid by the person for the year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings is less than the amount of the premium so required to be paid, the self-employed person shall pay to the Receiver General interest, at a rate per year prescribed by regulation made under subsection (5), on the difference between those amounts from the balance-due day for the year to the day of payment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.26(1) (src:2615)
GIVEN `the premium required to be paid for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid on or before the balance-due day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.26(1) the difference on which interest is payable` IS
    max 0 (`the premium required to be paid for the year` MINUS `the amount paid on or before the balance-due day`)

-- src:2615 | 152.26 (1) If the amount paid by a self-employed person on or before the person’s balance-due day for a year on account of the premium required to be paid by the person for the year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings is less than the amount of the premium so required to be paid, the self-employed person shall pay to the Receiver General interest, at a rate per year prescribed by regulation made under subsection (5), on the difference between those amounts from the balance-due day for the year to the day of payment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.26(1) (src:2615)
GIVEN `the balance-due day for the year` IS A DATE
      `the day of payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 152.26(1) the period for which interest is payable` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the balance-due day for the year`, `the day of payment`

-- Subsection (2): in addition to (1), a person who has failed to pay all or part of an instalment required by s 152.25 pays
-- interest on the amount from the day on or before which payment was required to the day of payment or the beginning of the
-- period for which interest is payable under (1), whichever is earlier.
-- src:2617 | (2) In addition to any interest payable under subsection (1), if a self-employed person, being required by section 152.25 to pay a part or instalment of a premium, has failed to pay all or any part of a premium as required, the person shall, on payment of the amount the person failed so to pay, pay to the Receiver General interest on the amount, at a rate per year prescribed by regulation made under subsection (5), from the day on or before which the person was required to make the payment to the day of payment or the beginning of the period in respect of which the person is liable to pay interest on the amount under subsection (1), whichever is earlier.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.26(2) (src:2617)
GIVEN `the instalment the person was required to pay` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of it that was paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on or before which the instalment was required to be paid` IS A DATE
      `the day of payment` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period for which interest is payable under subsection (1) begins, if there is one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 152.26(2) the period for which interest on the unpaid instalment is payable` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the day on or before which the instalment was required to be paid`, `the earlier day`
    WHERE
        `the earlier day` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the period for which interest is payable under subsection (1) begins, if there is one`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day of payment`
            WHEN JUST b THEN `the earlier of` `the day of payment` b

-- src:2617 | (2) In addition to any interest payable under subsection (1), if a self-employed person, being required by section 152.25 to pay a part or instalment of a premium, has failed to pay all or any part of a premium as required, the person shall, on payment of the amount the person failed so to pay, pay to the Receiver General interest on the amount, at a rate per year prescribed by regulation made under subsection (5), from the day on or before which the person was required to make the payment to the day of payment or the beginning of the period in respect of which the person is liable to pay interest on the amount under subsection (1), whichever is earlier.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.26(2) (src:2617)
GIVEN `the instalment the person was required to pay` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of it that was paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.26(2) the amount of the instalment on which interest is payable` IS
    max 0 (`the instalment the person was required to pay` MINUS `the amount of it that was paid`)

-- Subsection (3), farmers: for (2) the person is deemed to have been liable to pay on or before 31 December the part computed by
-- reference to whichever of (a) the premium for the year, (b) the premium for the preceding year, (c) the instalment stated in
-- the Minister's notice, if any, gives the least amount (two thirds of (a) or of (b), as s 152.25(2) says).
-- src:2619 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), if a self-employed person is required by subsection 152.25(2) to pay a part or instalment of a premium in respect of their self-employed earnings, the person is deemed to have been liable to pay on or before the day referred to in that subsection a part or instalment computed by reference to whichever of the following that gives rise to the least amount required to be paid by the person on or before that day:
-- src:2620 | (a) the premium required to be paid by them for the year in respect of their self-employed earnings;
-- src:2621 | (b) the premium required in respect of their self-employed earnings for the preceding year; or
-- src:2622 | (c) the amount stated to be the amount of the instalment payable by them for the year in the notice, if any, sent to them by the Minister of National Revenue.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.26(3) (src:2619-2622)
GIVEN `the premium required to be paid for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium required for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount stated to be the amount of the instalment payable for the year in the notice sent by the Minister of National Revenue, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.26(3) the instalment on which interest is calculated for a farmer` IS
    CONSIDER `the amount stated to be the amount of the instalment payable for the year in the notice sent by the Minister of National Revenue, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN min `two thirds of the premium for the year` `two thirds of the premium for the preceding year`
    WHEN JUST n THEN min n (min `two thirds of the premium for the year` `two thirds of the premium for the preceding year`)
    WHERE
        `two thirds of the premium for the year` MEANS (2 DIVIDED BY 3) TIMES `the premium required to be paid for the year`
        `two thirds of the premium for the preceding year` MEANS (2 DIVIDED BY 3) TIMES `the premium required for the preceding year`

-- Subsection (4), other persons: on each instalment day the person is deemed liable for the part computed by reference to
-- whichever of (a) the premium for the year, (b) the amounts of s 152.25(3)(b), (c) the amounts stated in the Minister's notices,
-- (d) the premium for the preceding year gives the least total of the instalments required by that day. K is the number of the
-- instalment day, 1 for 15 March to 4 for 15 December.
-- src:2624 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (2), if a self-employed person is required by subsection 152.25(3) to pay a part or instalment of a premium in respect of their self-employed earnings, the person is deemed to have been liable to pay on or before each day referred to in that subsection a part or instalment computed by reference to whichever of the following that gives rise to the least total amount of those parts or instalments required to be paid by them by that day:
-- src:2625 | (a) the premium required to be paid by them for the year in respect of their self-employed earnings;
-- src:2626 | (b) the amounts determined under paragraph 152.25(3)(b) in respect of them for the year;
-- src:2627 | (c) the amounts stated to be the amounts of instalment payable by them for the year in the notices, if any, sent to them by the Minister of National Revenue; or
-- src:2628 | (d) the premium required in respect of their self-employed earnings for the preceding year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.26(4) (src:2624-2628)
GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
      `the premium required to be paid for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium required for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium required for the second preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the amounts stated in the notices sent by the Minister of National Revenue as instalments payable by that day, if there are notices` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.26(4) the least total of the instalments required by the instalment day` IS
    CONSIDER `the total of the amounts stated in the notices sent by the Minister of National Revenue as instalments payable by that day, if there are notices`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN min `the total by reference to (a) and (d)` `the total by reference to paragraph 152.25(3)(b)`
    WHEN JUST n THEN min n (min `the total by reference to (a) and (d)` `the total by reference to paragraph 152.25(3)(b)`)
    WHERE
        `the total by reference to (a) and (d)` MEANS
            min ((k DIVIDED BY 4) TIMES `the premium required to be paid for the year`) ((k DIVIDED BY 4) TIMES `the premium required for the preceding year`)
        `the excess of the preceding year over half the second preceding year` MEANS
            max 0 (`the premium required for the preceding year` MINUS ((1 DIVIDED BY 2) TIMES `the premium required for the second preceding year`))
        `the total by reference to paragraph 152.25(3)(b)` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF k AT MOST 1 THEN (1 DIVIDED BY 4) TIMES `the premium required for the second preceding year`
                IF k EQUALS 2 THEN (1 DIVIDED BY 2) TIMES `the premium required for the second preceding year`
                IF k EQUALS 3 THEN ((1 DIVIDED BY 2) TIMES `the premium required for the second preceding year`) PLUS ((1 DIVIDED BY 2) TIMES `the excess of the preceding year over half the second preceding year`)
                OTHERWISE ((1 DIVIDED BY 2) TIMES `the premium required for the second preceding year`) PLUS `the excess of the preceding year over half the second preceding year`

§ `152.27 Penalties`

-- Subsection (1): a self-employed person who fails to file a return as and when required by s 152.22 is liable to a penalty of
-- 5% of the part of the premium for the year that remained unpaid at the expiry of the time the return was required to be
-- filed. If the person is liable to a penalty under s 162(1) or (2) of the Income Tax Act for the year, the Minister of
-- National Revenue may reduce the penalty or remit it in whole or in part.
-- src:2632 | 152.27 (1) Every self-employed person who fails to file a return of their self-employed earnings for a year as and when required by section 152.22 is liable to a penalty of five per cent of the part of the amount of the premium required to be paid by them for the year that remained unpaid at the expiry of the time the return was required to be filed, except that, if that person is liable to a penalty under subsection 162(1) or (2) of the Income Tax Act in respect of the year, the Minister of National Revenue may reduce the penalty to which the person is liable under this section or may remit the penalty in whole or in part.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.27(1) (src:2632)
GIVEN `the person fails to file a return of their self-employed earnings for the year as and when required by section 152.22` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the premium required for the year that remained unpaid at the expiry of the time the return was required to be filed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.27(1) the penalty for failing to file a return` IS
    IF `the person fails to file a return of their self-employed earnings for the year as and when required by section 152.22`
    THEN 5% TIMES `the part of the premium required for the year that remained unpaid at the expiry of the time the return was required to be filed`
    ELSE 0

-- src:2632 | 152.27 (1) Every self-employed person who fails to file a return of their self-employed earnings for a year as and when required by section 152.22 is liable to a penalty of five per cent of the part of the amount of the premium required to be paid by them for the year that remained unpaid at the expiry of the time the return was required to be filed, except that, if that person is liable to a penalty under subsection 162(1) or (2) of the Income Tax Act in respect of the year, the Minister of National Revenue may reduce the penalty to which the person is liable under this section or may remit the penalty in whole or in part.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.27(1) (src:2632)
GIVEN `the person is liable to a penalty under subsection 162(1) or (2) of the Income Tax Act in respect of the year` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the Income Tax Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.27(1) the Minister of National Revenue may reduce or remit the penalty` IF
    `the person is liable to a penalty under subsection 162(1) or (2) of the Income Tax Act in respect of the year`

-- Subsection (2): a person who fails to file a return as required by s 152.22(3) is liable to a penalty of $5 for each day of
-- default, to a maximum of $50.
-- src:2634 | (2) Every person who fails to file a return as required by subsection 152.22(3) is liable to a penalty of $5 for each day of default, to a maximum of $50.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.27(2) (src:2634)
GIVEN `the number of days of default in filing the return required by subsection 152.22(3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.27(2) the penalty for failing to file a return required by subsection 152.22(3)` IS
    min (5 TIMES `the number of days of default in filing the return required by subsection 152.22(3)`) 50

§ `152.28 and 152.29 The Income Tax Act, and the order of payments`

-- Subsection (1): subject to this Part and to regulations under (2), the provisions of Divisions I and J of Part I of the Income
-- Tax Act on payment of tax, assessments, objections, appeals, interest, penalties and excess refunds, and of Part XV (except
-- section 221) and subsections 248(7) and (11), apply, with the necessary modifications, to the premium as if it were tax.
-- src:2636 | 152.28 (1) Subject to this Part and except as otherwise provided by regulation made under subsection (2), the provisions of Divisions I and J of Part I of the Income Tax Act with respect to payment of tax, assessments, objections to assessments, appeals, interest, penalties and excess refunds, and the provisions of Part XV of that Act (except section 221) and subsections 248(7) and (11) of that Act apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, in relation to any amount paid or payable as or on account of the premium for a year in respect of self-employed earnings as though that amount were an amount paid or payable as or on account of tax under that Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.28(1) (src:2636)
GIVEN `the provision is one of Divisions I and J of Part I of the Income Tax Act with respect to payment of tax, assessments, objections to assessments, appeals, interest, penalties and excess refunds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is one of Part XV of that Act (except section 221) or subsection 248(7) or (11) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Part provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a regulation made under subsection (2) provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 152.28(2); none found in the Regulations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.28(1) the provision of the Income Tax Act applies to the premium as though it were tax` IF
        (   `the provision is one of Divisions I and J of Part I of the Income Tax Act with respect to payment of tax, assessments, objections to assessments, appeals, interest, penalties and excess refunds`
         OR `the provision is one of Part XV of that Act (except section 221) or subsection 248(7) or (11) of that Act`)
    AND NOT (`this Part provides otherwise`)
    AND NOT (`a regulation made under subsection (2) provides otherwise`)

-- Section 152.29: where a payment is made to the Minister of National Revenue on account of the taxes in s 228 of the Income Tax
-- Act and of a premium under this Part, despite any direction by the payer, the part of the payment that s 228 would apply to
-- tax is, subject to s 37 of the Canada Pension Plan, applied to the premium and deemed paid on account of it, and does not
-- discharge tax to that extent; what remains is applied to tax. The part is an input (s 228 is the Income Tax Act's).
-- src:2642 | 152.29 If any payment is made by a person to the Minister of National Revenue on account of taxes specified in section 228 of the Income Tax Act and of a premium under this Part in respect of self-employed earnings, despite any direction made by the person making the payment with respect to its application, the part of the payment that would be applied under that section in payment of tax under the Income Tax Act is, subject to section 37 of the Canada Pension Plan, to be applied in payment of a premium under this Part and is deemed to be a payment on account of the premium, and to the extent of the amount so applied, does not discharge liability for tax under the Income Tax Act, and any amount then remaining is to be applied in payment of tax under the Income Tax Act and discharges the liability of the person making the payment for that tax to the extent of that amount.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.29 (src:2642)
GIVEN `the part of the payment that would be applied under section 228 of the Income Tax Act in payment of tax` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: the Income Tax Act s 228, the Canada Pension Plan s 37
      `the premium owing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.29 the part of the payment applied in payment of the premium` IS
    min `the part of the payment that would be applied under section 228 of the Income Tax Act in payment of tax` `the premium owing`

-- src:2642 | 152.29 If any payment is made by a person to the Minister of National Revenue on account of taxes specified in section 228 of the Income Tax Act and of a premium under this Part in respect of self-employed earnings, despite any direction made by the person making the payment with respect to its application, the part of the payment that would be applied under that section in payment of tax under the Income Tax Act is, subject to section 37 of the Canada Pension Plan, to be applied in payment of a premium under this Part and is deemed to be a payment on account of the premium, and to the extent of the amount so applied, does not discharge liability for tax under the Income Tax Act, and any amount then remaining is to be applied in payment of tax under the Income Tax Act and discharges the liability of the person making the payment for that tax to the extent of that amount.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.29 (src:2642)
GIVEN `the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the payment applied in payment of the premium` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.29 the part of the payment left to be applied in payment of tax under the Income Tax Act` IS
    `the payment` MINUS `the part of the payment applied in payment of the premium`

§ `152.3 Refund of excess premium`

-- Subsection (1)(a): if the person has paid more than the premium, the Minister of National Revenue may refund the excess on
-- sending the notice of assessment, without any application.
-- src:2644 | 152.3 (1) If a self-employed person has paid, on account of the premium they are required to pay for a year in respect of their self-employed earnings, an amount in excess of the premium, the Minister of National Revenue
-- src:2645 | (a) may refund that part of the amount so paid in excess of the premium on sending the notice of assessment of the premium, without any application having been made for the refund; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.3(1)(a) (src:2644-2645)
GIVEN `the amount paid on account of the premium for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium the person is required to pay for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.3(1) the excess of the amount paid over the premium` IS
    max 0 (`the amount paid on account of the premium for the year` MINUS `the premium the person is required to pay for the year`)

-- Subsection (1)(b): the Minister shall make the refund after sending the notice of assessment if the person applies in writing
-- not later than three years after the end of the year.
-- src:2644 | 152.3 (1) If a self-employed person has paid, on account of the premium they are required to pay for a year in respect of their self-employed earnings, an amount in excess of the premium, the Minister of National Revenue
-- src:2646 | (b) shall make the refund after sending the notice of assessment, if an application for the refund is made in writing by the self-employed person not later than three years after the end of the year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.3(1)(b) (src:2644) (src:2646)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the excess of the amount paid over the premium` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister of National Revenue has sent the notice of assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has applied in writing for the refund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the application was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.3(1)(b) the Minister of National Revenue shall make the refund` IF
        `the excess of the amount paid over the premium` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the Minister of National Revenue has sent the notice of assessment`
    AND `the person has applied in writing for the refund`
    AND `the day on which the application was made` AT MOST `add years` (YMD `the year` 12 31) 3

